# Cost and model routing

Provider policy: see `00-clinicbridge-project-context.mdc`. Do not change the production provider or runtime model config unless explicitly instructed.

## Cursor engineering (agent model choice)

| Tier | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| Flash | Formatting, renames, small copy, simple isolated UI |
| Pro Low | Bounded features, standard bugs, tests, known-pattern refactors |
| Pro High | Architecture, uncertain RCA, cross-cutting state, security, tenant isolation, migrations, critical prod failures |

## ClinicBridge runtime

- Do not default to the most expensive model.
- Use the lowest-cost model that meets **measured** quality; escalate only on confidence, complexity, or risk.
- Deterministic validation is **identical** regardless of model.
- Stronger models do **not** get broader business permissions.
- Cache safe reusable reads; minimize prompt context; do not resend data already in structured state.
- Measure cost per **successful task**, not only per request.
